to-vaccine that prevents experimental auto-immune encephalomyelitis. <source>Eur. J. Immunol.</source> <volume>36</volume>:<fpage>2868</fpage>&#x02013;2874.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17048276</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yen, D., J. Cheung, H. Scheerens, F. Poulet, T. McClanahan, B. McKenzie, M.A. Kleinschek, A. Owyang, J. Mattson, W. Blumenschein, et al. <year>2006</year>. IL-23 is essential for T cell-mediated colitis and promotes inflammation via IL-17 and IL-6. <source>J. Clin. Invest.</source> <volume>116</volume>:<fpage>1310</fpage>&#x02013;1316.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16670770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fujino, S., A. Andoh, S. Bamba, A. Ogawa, K. Hata, Y. Araki, T. Bamba, and Y. Fujiyama. <year>2003</year>. Increased expression of interleukin 17 in inflammatory bowel disease. <source>Gut.</source> <volume>52</volume>:<fpage>65</fpage>&#x02013;70.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12477762</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Nielsen, O.H., I. Kirman, N. Rudiger, J. Hendel, and B. Vainer. <year>2003</year>. Upregulation of interleukin-12 and -17 in active inflammatory bowel disease. <source>Scand. J. Gastroenterol.</source> <volume>38</volume>:<fpage>180</fpage>&#x02013;185.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12678335</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">te Velde, A.A., F. de Kort, E. Sterrenburg, I. Pronk, F.J. ten Kate, D.W. Hommes, and S.J. van Deventer. <year>2007</year>. Comparative analysis of colonic gene expression of three experimental colitis models mimicking inflammatory bowel disease. <source>Inflamm. Bowel Dis.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>325</fpage>&#x02013;330.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17206675</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kotake, S., N. Udagawa, N. Taka